 "limits": [
  "three models trained on mixed-sex clinical CT, run on one CT of this donor: agreement between them is agreement between similar models, never anatomical confidence",
  "the muscle channel is TotalSegmentator total only, which has no thigh muscle label: the muscle prior is empty over most of the primary slices, as in version 1",
  "the fresh CT was acquired on a table and the block was frozen in another posture; the pelvis-fitted placement carries a measured per-structure error into every channel, and the distance channel carries it too (a shifted prior gives a shifted distance)",
  "the pelvis fit itself used Denver pelvis meshes, the source family of the reference; recorded, not removed",
  "the prior channels are inputs: the reference stays registry/cryo-tissue-map.json applied to the Denver original labels",
  "nothing here is anatomy",
  "prior_recall_of_reference is the fraction of Denver reference voxels of a class that the placed prior also calls that class; it mixes segmentation difference, placement error and posture, and separates none of them",
  "prior_on_labelled_other_tissue_fraction counts prior voxels of a class that fall on a Denver label of another class; prior voxels on ignore are counted apart because the tissue there is unlabelled, not negative",
  "the version 1 columns are the same measurement on data/derived/nlm-vhf/cryosections/block2/ct-prior-tissue.nii.gz; they compare two inputs, not two results"
 ],
